// The Tenerife + Canary Islands route cluster: airport-to-destination,
// intercity, cruise-port, and day-trip transfers.
//
// Core hub pages are NOT duplicated here:
//   - /tenerife/ + /es/tenerife/ (NEW CityRecord, mainAirportIata "TFS")
//   - /tenerife-south-airport-transfer/ + /es/traslado-aeropuerto-tenerife-sur/ (existing AirportRecord TFS)
//   - /santa-cruz-de-tenerife/ + /es/santa-cruz-de-tenerife/ (NEW CityRecord, mainAirportIata "TFN")
//   - /tenerife-north-airport-transfer/ + /es/traslado-aeropuerto-tenerife-norte/ (existing AirportRecord TFN)
//
// Two-airport architecture: Tenerife has two genuinely major, non-redundant
// airports (TFS serves the southern resort belt almost exclusively; TFN
// serves Santa Cruz/La Laguna and inter-island flights). Since
// CityRecord.mainAirportIata is 1:1, this cluster uses TWO CityRecords —
// matching the Bilbao/San Sebastián precedent exactly. Routes anchored at
// TFS/the southern resorts use originCitySlug "tenerife"; routes anchored
// at TFN/Santa Cruz use originCitySlug "santa-cruz-de-tenerife" (needed so
// AirportPageContent's `cities.find(c => c.mainAirportIata === iata)`
// resolution gives TFN's own hub page a working Related Transfers widget).
//
// Costa Adeje, Los Cristianos, Playa de las Américas, Puerto de la Cruz,
// Los Gigantes, and La Laguna have NO CityRecord of their own (matching the
// Vitoria-Gasteiz/Getxo/Hondarribia/Zarautz precedent from the Bilbao
// cluster) — they are covered as route-cluster destination pages only, not
// standalone hub pages, to avoid thin near-duplicate content competing with
// their own route pages for the same search intent.
//
// Per the spec's explicit instruction, NO per-hotel airport-transfer pages
// were built (unlike Zaragoza/Bilbao's hotel batches) — hotel/resort
// transfer logistics are covered as a genuine content section within each
// destination-level route page instead.
//
// NO inter-island route pages were built (Tenerife<->Gran Canaria/
// Lanzarote/Fuerteventura/La Gomera/La Palma) — a private car cannot
// physically cross to another island, so there is no genuine door-to-door
// service to sell here. Inter-island ferry (Fred Olsen Express, Naviera
// Armas from Los Cristianos) and flight (Binter Canarias/Canaryfly from
// TFN) options are mentioned as real local context within relevant route
// pages' prose, with zero dedicated "transfer" URLs implying an
// inter-island service that doesn't exist.
//
// Drive times throughout are hedged ("around"/"roughly") since online
// sources disagree by 10-20% on several Tenerife routes — figures were
// reconciled with this site's own existing published AirportRecord data
// (lib/airports/data.ts TFS/TFN entries) wherever an overlap existed.
//
// Uses the generic relationship engine (lib/routes/related.ts,
// lib/routes/coverage.ts) with zero city-specific logic.
//
